<http://data.silknow.org/object/5aed978d-08ca-3110-9fb7-1c360c86a5f0/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Dress panel of woven silk. Shaped panel of patterned cream silk showing a full width, selvedge to selvedge, plus two triangular panels seamed on either side. A sewn hem at the bottom suggests the original skirt hem. The top of the panel shows tailored shaping and the sides have been unpicked.\n\nThe high-quality silk is of cream-coloured silk satin with a repeating vertical pattern of four stems of bamboo or similar trailing canes with leaves and berries. These groups of plants are woven at intervals of 2 inches (5 cms) and there are three repeats in the natural fabric width. The pattern is picked out in a ribbed effect in pale pink and golden yellow silk."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/5aed978d-08ca-3110-9fb7-1c360c86a5f0> .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/5aed978d-08ca-3110-9fb7-1c360c86a5f0/dimension/4>
